Tip of Day Newsletter Clock Beater Are you looking for a health habit that turns back the clock? Recent research reveals that exercise may literally wipe away years of aging. In the study, a small group of middle-aged men who undertook a 6-month program of moderate exercise regained the level of cardiovascular fitness they had enjoyed as healthy 20-year-olds at the beginning of the study. The exercise program reduced their heart rates and improved the ability of their bodies to use oxygen. RealAge Benefit: Exercising regularly can make your RealAge as much as 9 years younger. To share the health with a friend, click here. Wednesday, November 21 Sponsor Find out moreabout this tip. Click here. Get free exercise help from RealAge.Check out My Fitness Plan. To rate this tip, please CLICK HERE. To change your e-mail address, CLICK HERE. To stop receiving the Tip of the Day, CLICK HERE or send a reply e-mail and type the word UNSUBSCRIBE in the subject line. Copyright© 2001, RealAge, Inc. All rights reserved. RealAge shall not be liable for any errors or delays in the content, or for any actions taken in reliance thereon. RealAge® is a federally registered trademark of RealAge, Inc. Age Reduction™ is a trademark of RealAge, Inc.